    "searchCoverage": "Official Email Routing REST uses Authorization Bearer API tokens against api.cloudflare.com/client/v4. GET /user/tokens/verify is the pinned User API Token validator. Destination addresses and zone routing rules are cheap authenticated reads. HTTP 200 bodies with a populated errors array are demoted via bodyErrorPaths. Dated incident search on 2026-09-13 found no current unresolved Email Routing API compromise.",
    "incidents": [
      {
        "date": "2017-02-17",
        "source": "https://blog.cloudflare.com/incident-report-on-memory-leak-caused-by-cloudflare-parser-bug/",
        "finding": "Cloudbleed: a Cloudflare HTML parser buffer overflow leaked memory (cookies, tokens, POST bodies) across customer traffic. Disclosed by Google Project Zero. Cloudflare patched the parser and reported no evidence of malicious exploitation.",
        "limitation": "Historical 2017 parser bug under the 2026-09-13 waiver. Not a current unresolved Cloudflare API compromise."
      },
      {
        "date": "2022-01",
        "source": "https://blog.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-investigation-of-the-january-2022-okta-compromise/",
        "finding": "Cloudflare investigated the January 2022 Okta compromise affecting its Atlassian environment. Cloudflare stated production systems serving customer traffic were not impacted.",
        "limitation": "Historical third-party identity-vendor incident. Not a current unresolved Email Routing / R2 / MCP API compromise."
      },
      {
        "date": "2025-08-12",
        "source": "https://www.theregister.com/2025/09/02/cloudflare_salesloft_drift_breach/",
        "finding": "Salesloft Drift campaign accessed Cloudflare's Salesforce tenant (support-ticket data) between 2025-08-12 and 2025-08-17. Cloudflare stated no Cloudflare services or infrastructure were compromised.",
        "limitation": "Historical third-party SaaS exposure. Not an api.cloudflare.com customer-token compromise. 2026-09-13 waiver keeps historical non-China incidents."
      },
      {
        "date": "2025-02-06",
        "source": "https://blog.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-incident-on-february-6-2025/",
        "finding": "R2 Gateway was inadvertently disabled during abuse remediation, causing a 59-minute R2 API availability outage. Cloudflare reported no loss or corruption of stored R2 data.",
        "limitation": "Historical availability incident, not a credential or data-exfiltration compromise."
      }
    ],
